From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 07:43:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] data: pass SAM's launch parameters on to the LuneOS launcher

SAM starts a native application with its launch parameters as one JSON
argument, and the Waydroid entry point dropped it. Nothing used it until
now: the first-start alert asks whether to download Android, and its answer
can only come back as a relaunch of Waydroid with parameters - an alert's
button is a luna call the shell makes on its own behalf, and nobody is told
it was pressed. The launcher tells that argument from a package name by its
leading brace.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS specific]
---
 data/scripts/waydroid-luneos.sh | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/data/scripts/waydroid-luneos.sh b/data/scripts/waydroid-luneos.sh
index 5a30563..9f788b2 100755
--- a/data/scripts/waydroid-luneos.sh
+++ b/data/scripts/waydroid-luneos.sh
@@ -1,2 +1,4 @@
 #!/bin/sh
-exec /usr/libexec/waydroid-luneos-app
+# SAM passes the launch parameters as one JSON argument; the launcher reads
+# them, so they have to reach it.
+exec /usr/libexec/waydroid-luneos-app "$@"
-- 
